{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Handoff state. Plan written with acceptance criteria, testing section and file_impact recorded; plan-review was RUNNING at handoff and the attestation still reads unsigned — check `rebar review-plan bc66-4827-355a-43bd --status` before assuming it needs a fresh run.\n\nThis is the epic's critical path: elfin-decagonal-polarbear (F11) depends_on it and cannot start until it lands.\n\nThe seam is chosen, not invented: the registry-validation cluster (_is_valid_reference, the six _check_* functions, _CHECKS, validate) calls only itself, takes routes as a PARAMETER and yields Finding — it reads the registry rather than building it. validate and Finding must stay importable from rebar._cli._registry, since test_capabilities, test_cli_registry and test_cli_registry_dispatch all import them from there; gate_dispatch.py's re-export of the plan_review_recovery cluster is the in-tree precedent."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788398846559419001,"uuid":"f3ec1772-b1a1-465c-8c28-b4c13b097c7b"}